\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {D}The operation swap with live attention patterns}{15}{appendix.D}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{app:qk}{{D}{15}{The operation swap with live attention patterns}{appendix.D}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces The frozen-vs-live attention probe for the operation swap (Section~\ref {sec:exp:swaps}): the paper-faithful chat configuration in fully-propagating mode with attention patterns frozen (top) vs.\ free to re-form (bottom). With live patterns the paper's exact outcome tokens appear (\emph  {little}, \emph  {pet}); frozen, nothing moves --- the swap's channel is QK-mediated. The en curves track the model's own chat answer ``tiny''; the top token past the crossover is \emph  {little} ($0.735$ at $15\times $).}}{15}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qk-probe}{{10}{15}{The frozen-vs-live attention probe for the operation swap (Section~\ref {sec:exp:swaps}): the paper-faithful chat configuration in fully-propagating mode with attention patterns frozen (top) vs.\ free to re-form (bottom). With live patterns the paper's exact outcome tokens appear (\emph {little}, \emph {pet}); frozen, nothing moves --- the swap's channel is QK-mediated. The en curves track the model's own chat answer ``tiny''; the top token past the crossover is \emph {little} ($0.735$ at $15\times $)}{figure.10}{}}
